# lib/

Project-private libraries. PlatformIO compiles each subdirectory here into a
static library and links it into the firmware; nothing needs to be listed in
`lib_deps`. Dependencies between them are resolved automatically, because each
library includes its neighbours by bare filename (e.g. `#include "storage.h"`).

## Libraries

| Directory | Status | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| `PulseSensor/` | Active, core | Pulse interrupts, debounce, kWh/rate derivation, runtime config globals |
| `Storage/` | Active | Persistence of pulses, config, and baseline in NVS via `Preferences` |
| `PulseLEDSim/` | Active (debug) | Drives a status LED on `LED_PIN` as a visual pulse indicator |
| `Display/` | Dormant | I2C character LCD output; not referenced by `src/main.cpp` |
| `Meter/` | **Empty placeholder** | Reserved for the planned refactor that moves meter state out of `PulseSensor` |

## `PulseSensor/`

The heart of the firmware, and currently the owner of all meter state.

- `pulseSensor.h` defines `SENSOR_PIN` (4), `DEBOUNCE_MILLIS` (50),
  `DEFAULT_PULSE_CONSTANT` (1600), `DEFAULT_RATE` (10.5).
- `pulseSensor.cpp` owns the storage for `volatile totalPulses`,
  `lastPulseTime`, and `rawFires`, plus `baselinePulses`, `baselineKwh`,
  `pulseConstant`, `utilityRate`, `safeKwhRead`, and `safeEstimateReading`.
- `readPulse()` is an `IRAM_ATTR` falling-edge ISR: it increments `rawFires`,
  drops edges inside the 50 ms debounce window, then increments `totalPulses`.
- `updateSafeKwh()` snapshots `totalPulses` with interrupts disabled and derives
  `safeKwhRead = totalPulses / pulseConstant` as a `double`.
- `updateSafeRate()` derives `safeEstimateReading = utilityRate * safeKwhRead`.

Note: `pulseSensor.cpp` defines `baselinePulses` and `baselineKwh` with the
`extern` keyword plus an initializer. It links today, but the cleaner form is a
plain definition in the `.cpp` and a bare `extern` declaration in the header —
expected to be cleaned up as part of the `Meter/` split.

## `Storage/`

All persistence goes through one `Preferences` namespace, `"sensorData"`.
`initStorage()` reads every value back into the globals in `PulseSensor/` at
boot and prints them to Serial.

| Key | Type | Written by |
|---|---|---|
| `totalPulses` | `ULong` | `savePulseCount()` |
| `pulseConstant` | `UShort` | `savePulseConstant()` |
| `utilityRate` | `Float` | `saveUtilityRate()` |
| `baselineKwh` | `Double` | `saveBaseline(kwh, pulses)` |
| `baselinePulses` | `ULong` | `saveBaseline(kwh, pulses)` |

Fallbacks used when a key is absent: `totalPulses` 0, `baselineKwh` 0.0,
`baselinePulses` 0, `pulseConstant` 1000, `utilityRate` 10.0 — note that the
last two differ from `DEFAULT_PULSE_CONSTANT` and `DEFAULT_RATE`.

## `PulseLEDSim/`

Implements `initLED()`/`pulseLED()`: two 5 ms HIGH/LOW blinks followed by a
200 ms pause on `LED_PIN` (18). It is a fixed pattern driven from `loop()`, not
a mirror of real sensor pulses, and it adds ~220 ms to every loop iteration.

## `Display/`

An I2C LCD driver (address `0x27`, geometry 24x4) that prints pulses, kWh, and
the pulse constant. It is not called from `src/main.cpp` and is effectively
parked. If it is ever re-enabled it needs fixing first: it includes
`"PulseSensor.h"` (wrong case — the file on disk is `pulseSensor.h`) and prints
`PULSE_CONSTANT`, a name that no longer exists in `pulseSensor.h`. Its
`LiquidCrystal_I2C` dependency is only declared in the `[env:uno]` block.

## `Meter/`

`meter.h` and `meter.cpp` exist but are empty (0 bytes). They are the start of
the refactor described in `PLAN.md`: give the meter its own type so baseline,
pulse constant, and kWh derivation stop living inside `PulseSensor`. Nothing
includes these files yet.
